toddlers, for the purpose of supplementing compensation
and training expenses for early childhood educators and
caregivers, improving staff retention and thereby ensuring
greater safety and consistency for children.
(ii) Eight percent (8%) on vouchers for families to
obtain care of their choosing through licensed childcare
centers, licensed family childcare homes, or license-exempt
care, prioritizing infant and toddler care.
(iii) Six percent (6%) on early childhood
mental/behavioral health services, including but not limited
